 least four hops (e.g. 695-800-933-362-1495). A cascade would therefore need four consecutive relay events each separated by <=600 time units. However, both endpoints are extremely sparse: 695 has 5 events with 5 distinct partners and 1495 has 4 events with 4 distinct partners across the entire 38,400-unit window (step_02), i.e. roughly one event per 8,000 units. With so few endpoint events and a required 4-link chain whose total latency budget is under ~2,400 units, there is no plausible time-respecting chain; the observed connectivity is an artefact of hub-mediated static reachability (the 800/933/274 hubs), not of an ordered, tightly-spaced influence path. I therefore judge the cascade absent, noting moderate confidence since I did not enumerate individual event timestamps along the candidate relay path."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.56,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Structurally, 695 and 1495 sit in disjoint 1-hop and largely disjoint 2-hop neighbourhoods. 695's direct partners in the window are 663, 800, 886, 918, 1468 (step_01), while 1495's are only 362, 701, 702, 1517 (step_03/step_04). None of these sets intersect, and the 2-hop expansions only meet through hubs such as 933/274/1531, so the shortest time-ignoring route is at least four hops (e.g. 695-800-933-362-1495). A cascade would therefore need four consecutive relay events each separated by <=600 time units. However, both endpoints are extremely sparse: 695 has 5 events with 5 distinct partners and 1495 has 4 events with 4 distinct partners across the entire 38,400-unit window (step_02), i.e. roughly one event per 8,000 units. With so few endpoint events and a required 4-link chain whose total latency budget is under ~2,400 units, there is no plausible time-respecting chain; the observed connectivity is an artefact of hub-mediated static reachability (the 800/933/274 hubs), not of an ordered, tightly-spaced influence path. I therefore judge the cascade absent, noting moderate confidence since I did not enumerate individual event timestamps along the candidate relay path.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 19260, "total_output_tokens": 2725, "total_tokens": 21985, "total_latency_ms": 43092, "llm_calls": 4, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}